==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|denken}}, from {{inh|de|goh|thenken, denken}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*þankijan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*þankijaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*teng-}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|denken}}, {{cog|nds|denken}}, {{m|nds|dinken}}, {{cog|fy|tinke}}, {{cog|en|think}}, {{cog|is|þekkja}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈdɛŋkən/|[ˈdɛŋkən]|[ˈdɛŋʔŋ̍]}}
* {{audio|de|De-denken.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-denken2.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-denken3.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-denken.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|denken<dachte,gedacht,dächte>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive|''[''{{m|de|an|tr=about}} + accusative'']''|rarely transitive}} to [[think]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''denke''', also bin ich.|I '''think''', therefore I am.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er '''denkt''' gewichtige Dinge.|He '''is thinking''' weighty thoughts.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''denke''' an früher.|I '''am thinking''' about the past.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with {{m|de|an}} + accusative}} not to [[forget]]; to [[remember]] (to bring along, etc.)
#: {{ux|de|'''Denk''' an den Schlüssel!|'''Don’t forget''' the key.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with reflexive dative}} to [[imagine]]
#: {{ux|de|Das kann ich mir '''denken'''.|I can '''imagine''' that.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''denke''' ihn mir als bärtigen Einsiedler.|I '''imagine''' him as a bearded hermit.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with reflexive dative}} to [[think]], to [[believe]], to [[assume]], to [[conjecture]]
#: {{ux|de|Ja, das '''dachte''' ich mir.|Yes, I '''thought''' so.}}

===Usage notes===
Denken originally took a genitive object (''ich denke deiner'' instead of ''ich denke an dich''). This usage is now archaic.

